own along the ____________.","options":["Both vertical and horizontal axis","horizontal axis","vertical axis","None of these"],"correctIndex":2,"page":216,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"},{"id":"el-b18-elq-5fc0a66c84521663","chapterId":"el-b18-c12","topicId":"el-b18-t1128-0","type":"mcq","text":"A _____________ is the representation of a frequency distribution.","options":["Mode","Mean","Histogram","Median"],"correctIndex":2,"page":216,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"},{"id":"el-b18-elq-ccbd6fe0f23eb960","chapterId":"el-b18-c12","topicId":"el-b18-t1128-0","type":"mcq","text":"A histogram is quit similar to _________________.","options":["Mean","Pie chart","Mode","Bar graph"],"correctIndex":3,"page":216,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"},{"id":"el-b18-elq-d5819b2c50ea6def","chapterId":"el-b18-c12","topicId":"el-b18-t1129-0","type":"mcq","text":"A data may or may not have a ______________.","options":["Median","Histogram","Mean","Mode"],"correctIndex":3,"page":222,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"},{"id":"el-b18-elq-f1a9e8a5e9944d2e","chapterId":"el-b18-c12","topicId":"el-b18-t1129-0","type":"mcq","text":"The ___________ is equal to the sum of all the values in the data divided by the number of values in the data.","options":["Frequency","Histogram","Mean","Central tendency"],"correctIndex":2,"page":222,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"},{"id":"el-b18-elq-7ece39e53b6ad278","chapterId":"el-b18-c12","topicId":"el-b18-t1129-0","type":"mcq","text":"____________ is defined as the value that occurs most frequently in the data.","options":["Mean","Frequency","Median","Mode"],"correctIndex":3,"page":222,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"},{"id":"el-b18-elq-e2d104e87a43ff59","chapterId":"el-b18-c12","topicId":"el-b18-t1129-0","type":"mcq","text":"A data can have more than ___________ mode.","options":["Three","one","None of these","two"],"correctIndex":1,"page":222,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"},{"id":"el-b18-elq-e31370af9637c801","chapterId":"el-b18-c12","topicId":"el-b18-t1129-0","type":"mcq","text":"There are _____________ methods of measuring central tendency.","options":["Two","Five","Three","One"],"correctIndex":2,"page":222,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"},{"id":"el-b18-elq-587935c8cb66cb3e","chapterId":"el-b18-c12","topicId":"el-b18-t1129-0","type":"mcq","text":"If the no of observation is even than no of values in the median is ______________.","options":["Five","Three","Two","one"],"correctIndex":2,"page":222,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"},{"id":"el-b18-elq-447aeedf9acd9994","chapterId":"el-b18-c12","topicId":"el-b18-t1129-0","type":"mcq","text":"In median first we arranged the data in _______________.","options":["ascending order","ascending or descending order","descending order","None of these"],"correctIndex":1,"page":222,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"},{"id":"el-b18-elq-2c96b17fe92aca53","chapterId":"el-b18-c12","topicId":"el-b18-t1129-0","type":"mcq","text":"______________ is used to divide the total no of observations in exactly two parts.","options":["Histogram","Bar graph","Mean","Median"],"correctIndex":3,"page":222,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"},{"id":"el-b18-elq-96aa7deaa4c3c729","chapterId":"el-b18-c12","topicId":"el-b18-t1129-0","type":"mcq","text":"Median is the middle value of the data, if it consists of ____________ of values.","options":["Prime number","odd number","composite number","even number"],"correctIndex":1,"page":222,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"},{"id":"el-b18-elq-3bb87025533193d7","chapterId":"el-b18-c12","topicId":"el-b18-t1129-0","type":"mcq","text":"Measure of central tendency allows us to represent our data using _____________ number.","options":["Five","One","Three","Two"],"correctIndex":1,"page":222,"difficulty":2,"source":"elearn"}]}